  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feasibility Study for Establishment of Smart Intelligent Transport System(ITS) in Lima and Chancay, Peru</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a feasibility study for the establishment of a smart Intelligent Transport System (ITS) for the integrated control of disaster situations and traffic accidents along the 133.2 km section between Lima and Chancay in Peru. The main scope of work includes status surveys and data analysis, analysis of similar projects, basic design, preparation of an implementation plan, cost estimation, feasibility analysis, and capacity building for local ITS experts.
Based on this project, it is expected to strengthen safety by reducing traffic accidents along the target corridor, reduce social costs by improving mobility, and lay the foundation for the promotion of ITS.</narrative>
  </description>
